This is a lammps to amber converter

beware that you always need to check the forcefield, if you want to edit it afterwards adjust the .frcmod and .lib file to your needs.

Prerequisites:
openbabel
ambertools

You need to export the home and the path like this:

export PATH=/path/to/your/uff2amberfolder:$PATH
export LAMMPS2AMBERHOME=/path/to/your/uff2amberfolder

for example if it is in ~/software/lammps2amber

export PATH=~/software/lammps2amber:$PATH
export LAMMPS2AMBERHOME=~/software/lammps2amber


then all should be set up to run the example in examples ZIF-8

just type:

uff4mof_to_amber.sh ZIF-8

and it should generate all the files from the ZIF-8.data and ZIF-8.cif


If you need more types than adjust the mapping
in fill_frcmod.py the mapping is defined:

ATOM_MAP = {
    "C_R": "CR",
    "C_3": "C3",
    "H_": "H",
    "N_R": "NR",
    "Zn3f2": "Zn",
}

adjust this as needed for you molecule. beware that amber types are only allowed to be 2 characters long.

also mind that the system should not exceed 1200 atoms per type, as amber needs unique atom names

if you have any problems or need more type mapping, feel free to contact me
